neutron: winewayland: letter keys take the VK of the letter they type (Colemak, Workman, Belgian, Czech, ...) [opt-in]

OPT-IN (his C353, 11-15): a fix built by emulating one reporter's environment ships to that reporter first. This
change is OFF unless NEUTRON_LAYOUT_VKEYS=1; unset (or any other value) = exactly the position tables of 187. On 206 it
was default-on and, combined with a VK/character table mismatch on his desktop, made typing QWERTY too (see
event-vkey-active-layout); enable it only together with NEUTRON_EVENT_VKEY=1.

Neutron#55 (@monkeysk4nk, US Colemak-DH on KDE Plasma 6.8.2 Wayland, runtime 11.10-187), his words:
  "I noticed an issue with indesign it never seem to have the correct layout, when typing or using ctrl + key.
   Illustrator on the other end it only has the wrong layout on ctrl + key. if I type some text or use letters for
   shortcuts without the CTRL all is good it matches my keyboad layout. Lastly Photoshop works perfectly with my
   layout, ctrl + keys work and all."
  "In both ctrl V works fine, because V is in the same spot I think. Ctrl S gives me the equivalent of ctrl D (place)
   which is in line with a qwerty keyboard. Ctrl Z paste in illustrator, and opens "text frame option" in indesign."
  "ctrl Z seems to paste at the back in illustrator so ctrl b, like qwerty."

Mechanism: add_xkb_layout() builds the scancode->VK table from fixed position tables chosen by the layout's
language (qwerty / azerty / qwertz, plus "dvorak" by name). KDE's "English (Colemak-DH)" is xkb us(colemak_dh):
language en-US -> the QWERTY table, so every key got the VK of its US-QWERTY position while its characters came
from xkb. The Colemak S key (<AC03>, QWERTY D) arrived as VK_D carrying 's'; the Z key (<AB05>, QWERTY B) as VK_B;
V stays on <AB04> = VK_V. Accelerator tables and apps that match Ctrl+letter by VK (Illustrator, InDesign, Win32
TranslateAccelerator) therefore ran Ctrl+D (InDesign Place, Illustrator Transform Again) and Ctrl+B (InDesign Text
Frame Options, Illustrator Paste in Back); typed text (WM_CHAR) was right. VkKeyScanEx('s') returned VK_D.

Windows: "The keyboard device driver receives scan codes from the keyboard, which are sent to the keyboard layout
where they are translated" and the scan code "identifies the key pressed regardless of the active keyboard layout",
while VKs are what apps use (learn.microsoft.com/windows/win32/inputdev/about-keyboard-input, "Keyboard Input Model",
"Scan Codes"). Each layout DLL carries its own scancode->VK table (KBDTABLES.pusVSCtoVK, kbd.h); kbdfr gives the
AZERTY A key VK_A and kbdgr the QWERTZ Z key VK_Z (Wine's azerty/qwertz tables copy them), and the reporter's own
Windows experience (Ctrl+S saves with Colemak-DH) shows the Colemak layout gives its S key VK_S - letter keys carry the
VK of the letter they type. (Colemak's KLID/table not measured on a Windows box: INFERRED from his report + MSKLC.) winex11.drv does the same by matching each key's characters against its layout
tables (X11DRV_InitKeyboard).

Change: after the position table (and patch zzzzzzzzzzzzzm's control-key keysym remap), a character key (position VK
A-Z or OEM) whose base keysym is a Latin letter takes that letter's VK (keys at letter positions claim first; a
second key typing the same letter, e.g. Colemak-DH's <LSGT> z, keeps its own VK). A key left on a letter VK another
key now holds takes the US OEM VK of its character (';' -> VK_OEM_1, ',' -> VK_OEM_COMMA, ...) when free, else a
position VK the letters freed. Non-Latin keys (Cyrillic, Greek, ...) keep the position VKs, as Windows' Russian or
Greek layouts do; digits, keypad, function and control keys are untouched. QWERTY, AZERTY, QWERTZ and Dvorak
produce the same tables as before. No per-app logic.

Not covered: the HKL still says 0409 (US) for Colemak - Windows would report a custom KLID (e.g. a0000409) for an
MSKLC layout; apps that special-case "US layout" by HKL see US. OEM keys of non-US Latin layouts keep the existing
tables' positions (only displaced keys are re-derived). i386-unix winewayland.so (32-bit apps) not rebuilt in the lab.
A second layout or a layout whose language differs from the user locale needs the companion patch
(event-thread-hkl): without it events are translated with the event thread's table.

Lab (agent kb55, nested KWin 6.8.2, xkb set per desk via XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT/VARIANT, keys sent by evdev code through
fake_input; probe kbt.exe logs WM_KEYDOWN VK/scan, WM_CHAR, ToUnicodeEx, an accelerator table Ctrl+S/Z/V/D/B,
MapVirtualKeyEx and VkKeyScanEx; base = 204's tree, pristine winewayland.so byte-identical to runtime 204's):
- us(colemak_dh): 204 n=3 and kill switch n=2 on the patched build: S key -> VK_D, accel Ctrl+D; Z key -> VK_B,
  accel Ctrl+B. Patched (11.10-204kb n=3, 204kc n=2): S key -> VK_S accel Ctrl+S, Z key -> VK_Z accel Ctrl+Z, V ->
  VK_V, ';' (QWERTY P key) -> VK_OEM_1, VkKeyScanEx a-z identity; typed text identical in every arm.
- us (QWERTY), fr, de (en_US locale), ru,us (Alt+Shift toggle, both groups): event streams hash-identical across
  204, patched and kill switch, n=2 each.
- Apps on us(colemak_dh), runtime 11.10-204kc (this + event-thread-hkl), kill = both switches =0 on the SAME build
  (this patch alone decides these results: the event-thread change is a no-op for a single en-US layout under en_US):
  Illustrator 2026: Colemak Ctrl+S -> Save As dialog 1/1 measured (2nd run's Ctrl+S step blocked by a stray Rectangle
  dialog), Ctrl+Shift+S -> Save As 2/2; Colemak Ctrl+Z undid a drawn rectangle 1/1 (rect pixels 1075 -> 0). Kill 2/2 and
  plain 204 1/1: no Save As on Ctrl+S or Ctrl+Shift+S (Transform Again / transparency grid), rectangle stays after
  Ctrl+Z (1090 -> 1090, Paste in Back).
  InDesign 2026: patched 2/2: Ctrl+S -> "Save As", Ctrl+Z -> no dialog; kill 2/2: Ctrl+S -> "Place", Ctrl+Z -> "Text
  Frame Options" 1/2 (2nd: the new document was not yet frontmost). Ctrl+V: no dialog in every arm.
  Photoshop 2026 (control): Colemak Ctrl+N (Colemak N key) opened New Document on patched AND kill 1/1 each (Photoshop
  matches Ctrl+letter by character); Ctrl+S showed no save window within 15 s in EITHER arm (lab limit, same both).
  Premiere 2026 J/K/L, Ctrl+Z on QWERTY: NOT run; QWERTY event streams are hash-identical across 204/patched/kill (n=2).
Switch: NEUTRON_LAYOUT_VKEYS=1 enables it (opt-in); unset = position tables (= 187).
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
@@ -442,6 +442,120 @@
     return vkey;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON layout-letter-vkeys (Neutron#55): with US Colemak-DH, Ctrl+S opened Illustrator's/InDesign's Place
+ * dialog (Ctrl+D) and Ctrl+Z ran InDesign's Text Frame Options (Ctrl+B), while typed text was right. The tables
+ * above pick a VK by physical position and only know azerty/qwertz/dvorak, so every other layout that moves
+ * letters (Colemak, Workman, Belgian, Czech/Slovak/Hungarian QWERTZ, Turkish F, ...) got US-QWERTY position VKs:
+ * the Colemak "s" key arrived as VK_D carrying an "s" character. On Windows the layout DLL's scancode->VK table
+ * gives a letter key the VK of the letter it types (Colemak's S key is VK_S), and winex11.drv does the same by
+ * matching each key's characters. So a character key whose base keysym is a Latin letter takes that letter's VK;
+ * a key displaced from its letter VK takes the US OEM VK of its character (';' -> VK_OEM_1, ...) or a VK the
+ * letters freed. Non-Latin keys (Cyrillic, Greek, ...) keep the position VKs, as on Windows. Digits, keypad,
+ * function and control keys are untouched. OPT-IN: only with NEUTRON_LAYOUT_VKEYS=1; unset = position tables. */
+static BOOL layout_letter_vkeys_enabled(void)
+{
+    static int enabled = -1;
+    if (enabled < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_LAYOUT_VKEYS");
+        enabled = e && e[0] == '1' && !e[1];  /* opt-in until the reporter confirms (C353) */
+    }
+    return enabled;
+}
+
+static BOOL is_char_vkey(WORD vkey)
+{
+    vkey &= 0xff;
+    return (vkey >= 'A' && vkey <= 'Z') || (vkey >= VK_OEM_1 && vkey <= VK_OEM_3) ||
+           (vkey >= VK_OEM_4 && vkey <= VK_OEM_8) || vkey == VK_OEM_102;
+}
+
+static WORD keysym_letter_vkey(xkb_keysym_t keysym)
+{
+    if (keysym >= XKB_KEY_a && keysym <= XKB_KEY_z) return keysym - XKB_KEY_a + 'A';
+    if (keysym >= XKB_KEY_A && keysym <= XKB_KEY_Z) return keysym - XKB_KEY_A + 'A';
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static WORD keysym_oem_vkey(xkb_keysym_t keysym)
+{
+    switch (keysym)
+    {
+    case XKB_KEY_semicolon:    return VK_OEM_1;
+    case XKB_KEY_slash:        return VK_OEM_2;
+    case XKB_KEY_grave:        return VK_OEM_3;
+    case XKB_KEY_bracketleft:  return VK_OEM_4;
+    case XKB_KEY_backslash:    return VK_OEM_5;
+    case XKB_KEY_bracketright: return VK_OEM_6;
+    case XKB_KEY_apostrophe:   return VK_OEM_7;
+    case XKB_KEY_comma:        return VK_OEM_COMMA;
+    case XKB_KEY_period:       return VK_OEM_PERIOD;
+    case XKB_KEY_minus:        return VK_OEM_MINUS;
+    case XKB_KEY_equal:        return VK_OEM_PLUS;
+    case XKB_KEY_plus:         return VK_OEM_PLUS;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* Fills vkeys[keyc] for min_keycode..max_keycode: key_vkey(), then the letter pass described above. */
+static void layout_vkeys(struct xkb_keymap *xkb_keymap, xkb_layout_index_t xkb_group, const USHORT *scan2vk,
+                         unsigned int min_keycode, unsigned int max_keycode, WORD *vkeys)
+{
+    unsigned int keyc, pass;
+    unsigned int claimed[256] = {0}, used[256] = {0};
+    BOOL lettered[0x300] = {0};
+
+    for (keyc = min_keycode; keyc <= max_keycode; keyc++)
+        vkeys[keyc] = key_vkey(xkb_keymap, keyc, xkb_group, scan2vk, key2scan(keyc - 8));
+
+    if (!layout_letter_vkeys_enabled()) return;
+
+    /* pass 0: keys whose position VK is a letter claim first, then OEM-position keys (e.g. <LSGT>) */
+    for (pass = 0; pass < 2; pass++)
+    {
+        for (keyc = min_keycode; keyc <= max_keycode && keyc < ARRAY_SIZE(lettered); keyc++)
+        {
+            const xkb_keysym_t *keysym;
+            WORD vkey = vkeys[keyc] & 0xff, letter;
+
+            if (!is_char_vkey(vkey) || (vkey >= 'A' && vkey <= 'Z') != !pass) continue;
+            if (xkb_keymap_key_get_syms_by_level(xkb_keymap, keyc, xkb_group, 0, &keysym) < 1) continue;
+            if (!(letter = keysym_letter_vkey(keysym[0])) || claimed[letter]) continue;
+            claimed[letter] = keyc;
+            lettered[keyc] = TRUE;
+            if (letter != vkey)
+                TRACE("keyc %#04x: keysym %#x takes vkey %#04x (position vkey %#04x)\n", keyc, keysym[0], letter, vkey);
+            vkeys[keyc] = letter;
+        }
+    }
+
+    for (keyc = min_keycode; keyc <= max_keycode; keyc++) used[vkeys[keyc] & 0xff]++;
+
+    /* keys left on a letter VK another key now holds */
+    for (keyc = min_keycode; keyc <= max_keycode && keyc < ARRAY_SIZE(lettered); keyc++)
+    {
+        WORD vkey = vkeys[keyc] & 0xff, repl = 0;
+        const xkb_keysym_t *keysym;
+        unsigned int other;
+
+        if (lettered[keyc] || !(vkey >= 'A' && vkey <= 'Z') || !claimed[vkey] || claimed[vkey] == keyc) continue;
+        if (xkb_keymap_key_get_syms_by_level(xkb_keymap, keyc, xkb_group, 0, &keysym) >= 1)
+            repl = keysym_oem_vkey(keysym[0]);
+        if (repl && used[repl]) repl = 0;
+        for (other = min_keycode; !repl && other <= max_keycode && other < ARRAY_SIZE(lettered); other++)
+        {
+            /* a position VK given up by a key that took its letter */
+            WORD freed = key_vkey(xkb_keymap, other, xkb_group, scan2vk, key2scan(other - 8)) & 0xff;
+            if (lettered[other] && is_char_vkey(freed) && !used[freed]) repl = freed;
+        }
+        if (!repl) continue;
+        TRACE("keyc %#04x: displaced from vkey %#04x -> %#04x\n", keyc, vkey, repl);
+        used[vkey]--;
+        used[repl]++;
+        vkeys[keyc] = repl;
+    }
+}
+
 static void add_xkb_layout(const char *xkb_layout, struct xkb_keymap *xkb_keymap,
                             xkb_layout_index_t xkb_group, LANGID lang)
 {
@@ -455,6 +569,7 @@
     VK_TO_WCHARS8 *vk2wchars_entry;
     struct layout *layout;
     const USHORT *scan2vk;
+    WORD *vkeys;
     WCHAR *names_str;
     WORD index = 0;
     char *ptr;
@@ -502,6 +617,15 @@
     }
     if (strstr(xkb_layout, "dvorak")) scan2vk = scan2vk_dvorak;
 
+    if (!(vkeys = calloc(max_keycode + 1, sizeof(*vkeys))))
+    {
+        ERR("Failed to allocate memory for Xkb layout vkeys\n");
+        free(layout);
+        xkb_state_unref(xkb_state);
+        return;
+    }
+    layout_vkeys(xkb_keymap, xkb_group, scan2vk, min_keycode, max_keycode, vkeys);
+
     layout->tables.pKeyNames = layout->key_names;
     layout->tables.pKeyNamesExt = layout->key_names_ext;
     layout->tables.bMaxVSCtoVK = 0xff;
@@ -563,7 +687,7 @@
 
     for (keyc = min_keycode; keyc <= max_keycode; keyc++)
     {
-        WORD scan = key2scan(keyc - 8), vkey = key_vkey(xkb_keymap, keyc, xkb_group, scan2vk, scan);
+        WORD scan = key2scan(keyc - 8), vkey = vkeys[keyc];
         VSC_VK *entry = NULL;
 
         if (!(scan & 0xff) || !vkey) continue;
@@ -588,7 +712,7 @@
 
     for (keyc = min_keycode; keyc <= max_keycode; keyc++)
     {
-        WORD scan = key2scan(keyc - 8), vkey = key_vkey(xkb_keymap, keyc, xkb_group, scan2vk, scan);
+        WORD vkey = vkeys[keyc];
         VK_TO_WCHARS8 vkey2wch = {.VirtualKey = vkey}, caps_vkey2wch = vkey2wch;
         BOOL found = FALSE, caps_found = FALSE;
         uint32_t caps_ret, shift_ret;
@@ -657,6 +781,7 @@
     }
 
     xkb_state_unref(xkb_state);
+    free(vkeys);
 
     TRACE("Created layout entry=%p index=%04x lang=%04x id=%04x\n", layout, layout->index, layout->lang, layout->layout_id);
     list_add_tail(&xkb_layouts, &layout->entry);
